<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan loosens cap on overseas equities investment.</title>
<headline>Taiwan loosens cap on overseas equities investment.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-05-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's finance ministry said on Saturday it would raise the ceiling on single overseas foreign fund investment in the island's equities to US$50 million from US$20 million.</p>
<p>The liberalisation would take effect on June 2, the ministry said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;This measure will benefit the internationalisation and liberalisation of the stock market,&quot; the ministry said.</p>
<p>The central bank currently limits all foreign holdings in Taiwan's stock market to 25 percent of the bourse's total value.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (5080815)</p>
